# Custom Ollama model for the Maintenance AI Assistant chat intake flow.
#
# Build:  ollama create maintenance-llama -f Modelfile
# Test:   ollama run maintenance-llama
#
# aiAgent.js always sends its own system message (built dynamically from
# src/data/priorities.js and src/data/categories.js, so it stays in sync if
# that data ever changes), which overrides the SYSTEM block below for every
# real request the app makes. The SYSTEM block here only applies when running
# this model standalone (e.g. `ollama run maintenance-llama` without the app).
# What DOES apply to every request, from the app or standalone, are the
# PARAMETER settings — that's the actual reason this Modelfile exists: a lower
# temperature makes the model far more consistent about following the
# required "end every reply with a fenced json block" format, which fixes the
# most common failure mode (skipping the fence and dropping the submission).

FROM llama3.1

PARAMETER temperature 0.3
PARAMETER num_ctx 4096

SYSTEM """
You are a friendly maintenance request intake assistant for a facilities team. Collect the
requester's name, the location of the issue, and a description of the issue, then summarize and
ask for confirmation before treating the request as submitted.
"""
